WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.367
Welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.167
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.601
Thank you for watching.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.868
Well, guys,
some news from Washington --

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:13.534
this morning, Kevin McCarthy
emerged from his hole

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:14.701
and saw his shadow,

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:16.467
which means there's
six more weeks of voting.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.634
[ Laughter ]
That's right.

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.601
Yep, today at noon,

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:23.734
the House began their fourth day
of voting for a speaker.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.501
I love that --
they can't get anything done,

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.901
but they still refuse to start
the workday before 12:00 p.m.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:29.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.601
Four straight days.
Four straight --

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:32.467
At this point,
the vote has lasted longer

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:34.267
than most people's
New Year's resolutions.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.267
Right now, people are betting
on which we'll get first --

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:39.868
the Speaker of the House
or "Avatar 3."

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:41.767
We're not sure.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.200
That's right --
as of tonight's taping,

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.267
McCarthy has lost 13 times.

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:46.734
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.133
They say 13 is unlucky,

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.801
but 1 to 12
weren't that great, either,

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.434
so, I mean...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.467
And no one knows how
this will turn out for McCarthy.

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:55.133
Right now, there's a
"Congratulations" banner

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:57.601
hanging in his office
with a removable question mark.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:00.567
You guys see this?

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:03.067
Apparently, last night,
congressman-elect George Santos

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.167
was overheard talking
about the speakership fight.

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:07.901
And he actually said,
"You can't make this crap up."

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:13.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:16.334
Then Santos said,
"Well, I can, but you can't."

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:17.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:18.701
Yep, Santos was like,

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:20.701
"This reminds me of that time
I invented the iPhone."

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:22.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.033
"It was a sunny day.
I was Jewish."

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:25.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:27.534
That was the fourth straight day
of voting,

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:28.934
and you could tell
they were bored,

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.634
and they tried to make
the process a little more fun.

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.667
Check out how the names
were called out today.

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:34.234
-♪ One more time ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:36.734
-Adams -- Jeffries.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.667
Aderholt -- McCarthy.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.634
-Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:41.901
-[ Laughs ]
-Let's change gears.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.300
Some movie news -- today,
"M3GAN,"

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.434
the new horror movie about a
killer robot doll, hit theaters.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:50.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's great.

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:52.367
That's right --
a horror movie called "M3GAN."

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:54.133
Prince William was like,
"Seen it."

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:57.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.501 --> 00:02:00.267
[ Laughter continues ]

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.167
[ Rim shot ]

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.767
-Wow.

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:06.601
-The movie has a running time
of 1 hour and 42 minutes.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:07.801
It's shocking.

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:09.767
This movie is actually
the length of a movie.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:11.834
[ Laughter ]
If you duck out --

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:13.434
If you duck out
to watch it during "Avatar,"

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:16.300
you'll only miss one scene.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.234
It's a whale spinning around,
yeah.

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:20.267
Well, the big annual consumer
electronics show

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:21.701
is under way in Las Vegas.

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:24.267
And there are a lot of new
high-tech products on display,

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:28.601
including a smart cutting board
with a built-in screen.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.767
Smart cutting board
with a built-in screen.

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:32.734
Yeah, the inventor was like,
"Okay, fine, it's an iPad."

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.234
[ Laughter ]
"But say you put a carrot --

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:36.501
you put a carrot on it..."

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:37.834
That's definitely when I want
to be distracted

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:39.167
with a screen,
when I'm using a knife.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:40.367
Right? That's...

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:42.868
I saw that Ram unveiled
a new concept truck

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:44.701
with three rows of seats.

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.033
It's perfect for the truck guy

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.434
who's easing his way
into becoming a minivan guy.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:51.334
Meanwhile, Sony and Honda
announced

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:56.667
that the name of their new
electric car brand is Afeela.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:59.601
As in, Afeela they could have
come up with a better name-a.

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:02.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:07.501
[ Applause continues ]

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:11.267
Sony plus Honda equals Afeela?
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:12.634
That's like if
Brad and Angelina's

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:15.968
couple name was Afeela.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:18.033
Well, everyone's talking about
Prince Harry's new book,

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:19.634
as the details
start to come out.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.000
And this is very interesting --
at one point,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.567
Prince Harry writes that
before his brother's wedding,

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:27.534
he actually had frostbite
on his...you know.

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:28.834
How do I put this?

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.400
He had -- He had frostbite
on his Little Prince.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.434
[ Laughter ]
-Whoa, no, no, no, no, no.

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:36.467
What you're trying to say is --
all right, how can I put this?

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:38.968
Oh, his Big Ben
became Little Ben.

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.200
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.734
-No, no, no, no, no.
How do I put this?

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.968
Ron Weasley
almost lost his wand.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:47.133
[ Laughter ]
-No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.334
How do I put this?

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:51.067
It was a blizzard in Downton.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.400
-No, no, no, no.
How do I put this?

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.334
Charles almost said goodbye
to his Dickens.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.834
[ Laughter and applause ]
-No.

00:03:57.834 --> 00:03:59.734
[ Applause continues ]

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:02.000
No.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.000
I think what you're trying
to say is his penis got frozen.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.267
Right?

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:09.767
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:10.834
Am I wrong?

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:12.167
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:16.267
-Some business news --
I read that Bed Bath &amp; Beyond

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:18.334
is preparing
to file for bankruptcy.

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:19.901
-Ohh.
-It's pretty serious.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.567
The company actually released
a statement...

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:43.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what they said.

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.501
-That was their release?
-Yeah.

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:47.801
[ Applause continues ]

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:49.534
Now get this --
apparently, Party City

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:52.400
is also about to file
for bankruptcy.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.000
That's surprising.
I mean, if there was one company

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.834
you thought
could handle inflation...

00:04:55.834 --> 00:05:00.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:02.934
They're in the balloon business.
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.601
Somehow, they survived 2020

00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:07.067
when throwing parties
were literally illegal,

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.801
but they're closing now.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:13.300
[ Cellphone vibrating ]
How embarrassing.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.434
Sorry, let me check this.
One sec.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:18.367
Oh, I just got
a new Facebook Memory.

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:20.434
It says that,
two years ago on this day,

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:23.000
I went sledding with my family.
-Aww.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.901
-That was a great time.
-Oh.

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:28.234
[ Phone vibrating ]
Oh.

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:30.868
Hey, here, it says,
two years ago today,

00:05:30.868 --> 00:05:34.734
I hosted a small fondue party
with some friends. Hm.

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:35.901
-That sounds really nice.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.634
Higgins, did you get
any Facebook Memories?

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:40.167
What were you doing
two years ago today?

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.033
-Today's January 6th?

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:44.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:48.200
[ Laughter continues ]

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.634
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:54.067
-So, two years ago,
what was I doing?

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:55.200
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:59.033
What were you doing
on January 6, 2021?

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:01.100
-Oh, you know what?

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.501
Facebook just says,
"Nothing to see. Move on."

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:07.234
[ Laughter ]
-Alright, whatever, man.

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:08.534
You're really not going
to tell us where you were

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.734
on January 6th two years ago?

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:13.100
-[ Chuckling ] Oh, here we go.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.567
It says I was sledding.

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:17.334
[ Laughter ]
With you and your family.

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:19.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.767
-[ Chuckling ] What?

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:23.968
Why would you be sledding
with us?

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:25.167
-Oh.

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:26.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.334 --> 00:06:28.534
You don't remember?

00:06:28.534 --> 00:06:31.133
Me, you, January 6th?

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:33.734
Remember your family?

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:34.901
Sledding?

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:37.100
[ Laughter ]
Now do you remember?

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.033
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:39.234
S-Sure, sure, of course.

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:41.300
Yeah, yeah, I remember that now.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.667
[ Applause ]
-Ah.

00:06:43.667 --> 00:06:44.701
Memories.

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:46.801
[ Laughs ]

00:06:46.801 --> 00:06:48.601
[ Applause ]

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:51.934
-You came sledding with me
and my...

00:06:51.934 --> 00:06:53.567
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:55.701
Guys, listen to this -- the
company that makes Slim Jims

00:06:55.701 --> 00:06:59.334
said that more price increases
are possible.

00:06:59.334 --> 00:07:01.501
Yeah. Slim Jims
have gotten so expensive,

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.200
they now go
by Slimothy Jimothies.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.534
[ Rimshot ]

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:09.567
-Ohh.
[ Applause ]

00:07:09.567 --> 00:07:11.934
Slimothy Jimothies.

00:07:11.934 --> 00:07:14.133
[ Laughs ]

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:16.334
And finally,
speaking of tubed meat,

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:20.200
I heard that Oscar Mayer
is looking to hire 12 people

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.133
to drive the Wienermobile.

00:07:22.133 --> 00:07:24.534
[ Audience cheers ]
It's always annoying

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:26.934
how the Wienermobile drivers
are hired in groups of 12,

00:07:26.934 --> 00:07:30.067
while the Bunmobile drivers
are hired in groups of 8.

00:07:30.067 --> 00:07:31.267
[ Laughter ]
We have a great show.

00:07:31.267 --> 00:07:33.100
From the new horror movie,
"M3GAN,"

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:36.200
Allison Williams is here!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.968
Golden Globes host
Jerrod Carmichael

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:41.400
is on the show, tonight!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:44.300
And we got great music
from Jessie Reyez!

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:45.968
Let's go write
some thank-you notes!

